  "question": "What has been proposed to reduce the risk that rivalry between countries causes AI developers to overlook the dangers of deployment, and by what mechanism?",
  "reference_answer": "Use careful, deliberate communication in AI-governance publications, avoiding rhetoric that inflames relations between countries or portrays AI development as a contest in which only winning matters. The proposed mechanism is to avoid escalating international tensions and encouraging an overriding focus on competitive victory. This helps prevent a competitive spiral in which researchers disregard the risks of deploying unsafe AI systems.",
  "spans": [
    "At GovAI, we talk about being careful in our writing so that we don't necessarily escalate tensions between countries.",
    "There are people who want to drum up a potential AI arms race — people who say, “Competition is the only thing that matters.” And I think that's the type of dangerous rhetoric that we want to avoid.",
    "We don't want a race to the bottom where, whether it's the US, China, or the EU, researchers only care about \\[winning, and fail to consider\\] the potential risks of deploying AI systems that are not safe."
  ]
}
